finally had the screws and metals removed from leg, everything seems good, now enjoying a week-long (so far) of pretty bad case of stomach cramps, man will the summer adventures never end?, also solar eclipse it's just a week away, my first, excited

as for progress in the z80 front, i decided that just studying other people's code leaves too many proofs are left as exercises for the reader, so went ahead to downloaded some books and references on the z80, since then not a lot of tangible src code was made but still 'z80 assembly language programming' by leventhal is a comprehensive guide that already solved lots of nebulous concepts encountered (differences between hl or bc? etc), and more importantly, lots and of lots of exercises starting from zero to the very hard, designed to help you achieve proficiency with the z80 and it's assembler, i'm in the process of weed through them, it demonstrates again that the youtube tutorial industry archived little teaching stuff, seems nothing beats 700-pages books of computer literature from 1979
